From b7174a7bff2d8022d336fa720c3e649fbe8288ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koudai Aono <koxudaxi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 07:04:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] mellum: model config, memory and host contract

Recognition of general.architecture = mellum inside the QWEN4_EXP family,
hyperparameter and tensor validation that refuses each bad key or shape by
name (32 query heads over 4 KV heads, widths in 128s), Q8_0 binding, the
memory plan and session allocation with the forward entries refusing, the
ds4_engine_is_mellum predicate, the model's sampler defaults (1.0 / 1.0 / 0 /
0), and a false payload predicate with save and load refusing at every entry.

The model-free acceptance is tests/test_mellum_config.c on the sparse GGUF
that tests/mellum_fixture.h writes; the same binary validates and binds the
real Q8_0 GGUF when DS4_TEST_MELLUM_MODEL names it.

The series stays inline in ds4.c/ds4.h like the qwen35 series: the fork's
later "move the front ends to .inc files" refactor commits are not carried.

Upstream: not offered, fork only
Retire-when: upstream runs Mellum 2.1 with this host contract
Carried-commits: 83e39b63 0428a4c6 06b13f83 5b6758e0 1d9b6284 d3892ee1 7eef70be c9d63e08
